  "Question": "An American traveling in Italy wishes to exchange American money (dollars) for Italian money (lire). If \\(3000\\) lire \\(= \\$1.60,\\) how many lire will the traveler receive in exchange for \\(\\$1.00?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(180\\)",
    "B": "\\(480\\)",
    "C": "\\(1800\\)",
    "D": "\\(1875\\)",
    "E": "\\(4875\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "To find how many lire correspond to one dollar, divide the given number of lire by the given number of dollars:\n\\[\n3000\\div1.60=30000\\div16=1875.\n\\]\nThe middle expression multiplies both numbers in the division by \\(10\\), leaving the quotient unchanged. The traveler receives \\(1875\\) lire for \\(\\$1.00\\), choice D.",
